From 6e96ea4326de4cab6cc888c823f99e274179854c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 15:28:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 48/75] wm: deliver IS_GAME task metadata to the compositor

METADATA_IS_GAME was stamped but never usable, for two reasons:

  - setTaskMetadata() runs when the task SurfaceControl is built, which
    happens before any activity is attached. getTopNonFinishingActivity()
    returns null there, so nothing was ever classified as a game. This is
    the same trap IS_DIALOG documents, and it gets the same live re-stamp
    in prepareSurfaces().

  - A sideloaded game declares no android:appCategory, so PackageManager
    reports CATEGORY_UNDEFINED. The user-facing "Open with game control
    panel" toggle didn't help: ArcAppService.resolveAppCategory() only
    rewrites the category in the app list reported to Chrome, never in
    system_server's PackageManager. Task now also consults the
    fydroid_game_packages secure setting.

The package set is cached and primed from WindowManagerService.systemReady():
reading Settings from the surface-build path would put a ContentProvider
call under the WM lock, and at boot it would just cache an empty set with
no later change event to correct it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Icac5008342d4fd689ffd5ad0bc04174e701c4ec6
---
